					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctortronik" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3685285); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3685285&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608067212" alt="DoctorTronik" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3685285)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctortronik" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3685285); return false;" >DoctorTronik</a></span> <span class="odate time_1533584764 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">06 Aug 2018 19:46</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3901011">
									

<p>Wow, some people really have trouble letting themselves be entertained! Maybe to avoid chafing so many butts you could somehow make this more obviously an anart object, maybe commissioned from AWCY or&#8230; Something&#8230;? Some people have said this belongs on the J page; well, maybe some anartist made them as a joke, right? Dunno, just throwing it out there.</p>
<p>These actually reminded me of &quot;the glasses&quot; from <em>The Lost Room</em>, you know, the ones that let you set shit on fire. I'm pretty sure &quot;cool guys don't look at explosions&quot; came later, but I like to imagine there's a connection.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&#8230; detonated with the estimated force of a <strong>twenty megaton</strong> bomb. All on-location parties were killed, but due to the volatile nature of SCP-1143 this test had been conducted in a remote location&#8230;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>A <em>very</em> remote location! Great gravy!</p>
<p>+1</p>

